---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SKEPTICISM, ORG } from "../../config";
---
<Base
  title={SKEPTICISM.name}
  description="The Center's convening program on artificial intelligence and public life. Canada is Edition One."
>
  <div class="wrap phead">
    <h1>{SKEPTICISM.name}.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      The Center's convening program on artificial intelligence and public life, and the
      research it produces. Canada is Edition One.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>Skepticism is not opposition.</h2></div>
      <p class="dnote" style="margin-top:0;max-width:70ch;font-size:17px">
        It is the ordinary practice of asking an institution to show its work before
        granting it trust, applied to a technology that has mostly been exempted from it.
        The Center holds itself to the same test.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>What the program produces.</h2></div>
      <div class="prin">
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Convenings.</h3>
          <p>Editions that put researchers, policy staff, and builders in the same room on the same question. Canada opens the series.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Scorecards and playbooks.</h3>
          <p>Assessments that let someone outside an institution measure it against a standard it did not set, and step-by-step material for people who have to act.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Policy research.</h3>
          <p>Work aimed at the specific person who can change a rule, written so they can act on it without a translator.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="credo" style="padding:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:clamp(27px,3.4vw,40px);max-width:20ch">Edition One: Canada</h2>
      <p class="attr" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:58ch">
        Host institutions shape the agenda alongside the Center rather than sponsoring a
        finished one. Partners, hosts, and funders working on the same questions can write
        to <a href={`mailto:${ORG.email}`} style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5)">{ORG.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <a class="pill" href="/contact">Host or partner on Edition One &rsaquo;</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
